{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:87805",
  "title": "Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-24 12:04:09"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-24 19:12:26"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: netlabel: Fix NULL pointer exception caused by CALIPSO on IPv4 sockets (CVE-2025-22063)\n\n* kernel: calipso: Don't call calipso functions for AF_INET sk. (CVE-2025-38147)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: hda/cs35l41: Fix firmware load work teardown (CVE-2026-64481)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: seq: close a re-opened queue timer in the destructor (CVE-2026-68202)\n\n* kernel: vmxnet3: fix BUG_ON in vmxnet3_get_hdr_len() for Geneve packets (CVE-2026-68299)\n\n* kernel: ovl: check access to copy_file_range source with src mounter creds (CVE-2026-68448)\n\n* kernel: xfs: fix exchange-range reflink flag clearing issue with INO1_WRITTEN (CVE-2026-80530)\n\n* kernel: xfs: bounds-check buffer log item's dirty bitmap (CVE-2026-80536)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* RTLA segfaults on freed memory access on double SIGINT [rhel-9.8.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-193029)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
